  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Areas of frost tonight.\n\nWarm air advection in the wake of a surface ridge tonight, will \nsupport 850mb temperatures to climb into the upper single digits \nCelsius tonight. However, clear skies and light winds across the \nregion will likely support frost formation to form, especially for \nareas outside of the northern Niagara Frontier as there may be enough \nof a gradient wind to limit the areal extent of the frost. This \nbeing said a Frost Advisory is in effect tonight for Monroe, Wayne \nand northern Cayuga. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...An extended period of dry and warmer weather begins \nthis afternoon and likely lasts through the week.\n\nSurface high pressure will remain anchored over the eastern US this \nweek, that coupled with a ridge of high pressure aloft will maintain \nfair weather with afternoon temperatures near or above normal.",
